# Every text file is stored LF. Without this, a Windows tool that rewrites a
# whole file writes CRLF, `.prettierrc`'s `endOfLine: "auto"` then PRESERVES
# that CRLF on every later format run, and the file is committed with new line
# endings — so a ten-line change lands as a thousand-line diff nobody can
# review. `test/webview/ui-render.tsx` had already drifted this way and is
# normalised in the same commit as this rule; it was the only text file in the
# repo stored with CRLF.
#
# `text=auto` leaves binaries alone (git detects them), and the more specific
# rules below still win — a later matching pattern overrides an earlier one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Vendored JSON schemas are byte-pinned by tests
# (test/*.schema.vendored.test.js). Force LF on every platform so the sha256
# gate matches on a Windows checkout (where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# smudge them to CRLF on disk). The tests also normalize CRLF→LF defensively.
schemas/board.schema.json text eol=lf
schemas/system-manifest-v1.schema.json text eol=lf
# Vendored Kconfig symbol snapshot (gated by test/lsp.kconfig.test.js).
test/fixtures/alp-kconfig-symbols.txt text eol=lf
# Shell scripts must stay LF: with core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout
# smudges them to CRLF and bash fails on the trailing \r
# ("set: pipefail\r: invalid option name"), breaking pnpm run install:vscode
# and the curl|bash tan installer in media/tan-install/install.sh.
*.sh text eol=lf
